My favorite "conduct" is to have one only city, and make godly heros to go 
out and conquer all the nodes and ruins.

Picks are Artificer, Runemaster, Node Mastery, Alchemy.  This lets me 
actually gain mana by making and crushing magic items when I don't have 
anything better to do with my casting skill.  Also it allows me to make non-
optimal items for temporary use, then crush them when I make better ones.  

Alchemy is greatly underrated -- it turns the two main resources (gold and 
mana) into one.  This is incredibly useful.  In the early game, I use the 
mana profit from crushing items to pay the gold upkeep on my buildings;  in 
the late game taxes pay for spellcasting.

The remaining picks are LLCNNSS.  I rely on nodes, ruins, diplomacy, and 
libraries for research so I can increase casting skill as fast as possible.  


